# Transparent Proxy Bootstrap

This host routes normal outbound traffic through sing-box TUN to a user-provided
SOCKS5 or HTTP proxy endpoint.

Important distinction:

- Hetzner VM IPv4: used for SSH and initial bootstrap.
- Proxy egress IP: the fixed IP from the proxy provider, used for outbound traffic.

Configured proxy:

- mode: {{ proxy_mode }}
- endpoint: {{ proxy_host }}:{{ proxy_port }}
- expected egress IP: {{ proxy_expected_egress_ip }}

Direct-routing defaults:
{% for domain in proxy_direct_domain_suffixes %}
- {{ domain }}
{% endfor %}
- private IP traffic when `proxy_direct_private_traffic=true`
- TCP/{{ proxy_ssh_port }} ingress and reply traffic by port

Operational commands:

- `/usr/local/bin/verify-global-proxy`
- `/usr/local/bin/verify-transparent-proxy`
- `/usr/local/bin/check-dns-proxy`
- `sudo {{ proxy_update_script_path }} --mode socks5 --host <host> --port <port> --expected-ip <ip> --username <user> --password <password>`
- `sudo {{ proxy_rollback_script_path }}`

The proxy endpoint is tested directly before transparent routing is applied.
The observed direct-proxy egress IP must match `{{ proxy_expected_egress_ip }}`.
